## Chapter 3: Decision trees

This hand-in shows the layout of a report built from code. Every number below is made up from a formula; a real study would fill the replicates from its own runs.

Each setting was run with 5 seeds. Tables give the mean and the sample standard deviation over the seeds.

<a id="sec-2"></a>

### Chapter 3 / Exercise 1: Accuracy by tree depth

<a id="tbl-1"></a>

**Table 1.** Test accuracy and F1 by depth

| depth | test_accuracy | f1 |
| :--- | ---: | ---: |
| depth 2 | 0.7000 ± 0.0112 | 0.6600 ± 0.0112 |
| depth 4 | 0.7750 ± 0.0079 | 0.7350 ± 0.0079 |
| depth 8 | 0.8090 ± 0.0119 | 0.7690 ± 0.0119 |

*mean ± sample standard deviation over the usable seeds*

