## Chapter 4: Regression

<a id="sec-5"></a>

### Chapter 4 / Experiment 1: Accuracy against label noise

Accuracy fell as label noise rose. A least-squares line through the five noise levels:

<a id="tbl-4"></a>

**Table 4.** OLS of accuracy on label noise

| term | coef | std_err | t | p_value | ci_low | ci_high |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| const | 0.8150 | 0.0061 | 133.0889 | 0.0000 | 0.7955 | 0.8345 |
| noise | -0.8500 | 0.0500 | -17.0000 | 0.0004 | -1.0091 | -0.6909 |

*n = 5; R\^2 = 0.9897; adjusted R\^2 = 0.9863; F = 289.000, p = 0.0004; 95% intervals*

- the intercept is the accuracy without noise
- the slope is the accuracy lost per unit of noise

